  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF MONARCH BUTTERFLY HABITAT TOGETHER WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES, THROUGH CLIMATE CHANGE ADAPTATION AND MITIGATION EFFORTS EMBEDDED IN A DEVELOPMENT MODEL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONSERVE AND RESTORE THE FORESTS OF THE MONARCH BUTTERFLY BIOSPHERE RESERVE (MBBR) IN MEXICO BY WORKING WITH 15 INDIGENOUS AND EJIDO (COMMUNALLY OWNED LANDS) COMMUNITIES BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF HABITAT LOSS AND THE THREATS OF CLIMATE CHANGE (INCREASE IN TEMPERATURE, FOREST PLAGUES, AND FIRES, AND REDUCTION OF PRECIPITATION), EXPANSION OF THE AGRICULTURAL FRONTIER, AND LAND USE CHANGE. THROUGH THIS TWO-YEAR GRANT ALTERNARE, A.C. WILL: (1) PLACE 3,024 HA UNDER COMMUNITY- BASED FOREST MANAGEMENT (698 CORE ZONE, 2,326 BUFFER ZONE) (2) REFOREST 60 HECTARES IN THE BUFFER ZONE OF THE MBBR (3) TRAIN 30 LOCAL LEADERS ON CONSERVATION ANDSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT (4) TEACH SUSTAINABLE PRODUCTION AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT PRACTICES TO 300 FARMERS (5) PROVIDE TECHNICAL AND MARKETING SUPPORT TO 75 FAMILIES PARTICIPATING IN IN SIX SUSTAINABLE PRODUCTIVE PROJECTS. AND (6) HIRE A CONTRACTOR TO PERFORM AN EVALUATION OF ALTERNARES LEADERSHIP AND SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT TRAINING PROGRAM.</narrative>
  </description>
